#ASSERT `s 486.5(8.1) the judge or justice must inform the victims, witnesses and justice system participants of the order's existence and of their right to apply to revoke or vary it` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 486.5(8.2) the prosecutor must inform the judge or justice of what they have done` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 486.5(8.2) the prosecutor must inform the judge or justice of what they have done` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 486.5(8.2) the prosecutor must inform the judge or justice of what they have done` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 486.5(8.2) what the prosecutor informs the judge or justice of is complete` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 486.5(8.2) what the prosecutor informs the judge or justice of is complete` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- (9) no person shall publish the contents of an application, the evidence at a hearing, or any other identifying information, unless the judge or justice refuses to make an order
#ASSERT `s 486.5(9) the person is prohibited from publishing, broadcasting or transmitting what would be published` FALSE `s 486.5(9) the contents of an application` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 486.5(9) the person is prohibited from publishing, broadcasting or transmitting what would be published` FALSE `s 486.5(9) any evidence taken, information given or submissions made at a hearing under subsection (6)` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 486.5(9) the person is prohibited from publishing, broadcasting or transmitting what would be published` FALSE `s 486.5(9) any other information that could identify the person to whom the application relates as a victim, witness or justice system participant in the proceedings` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 486.5(9) the person is prohibited from publishing, broadcasting or transmitting what would be published` TRUE `s 486.5(9) the contents of an application` EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- the judge or justice refused to make an order
#ASSERT `s 486.5(9) the person is prohibited from publishing, broadcasting or transmitting what would be published` FALSE `s 486.5(9) something else` EQUALS NOTHING

§ `s 486.51 -- varying or revoking an order`
#ASSERT `s 486.51(1) the prosecutor must make an application to vary or revoke the order on the person's behalf` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 486.51(1) the prosecutor must make an application to vary or revoke the order on the person's behalf` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- no request
#ASSERT `s 486.51(1) the prosecutor must make an application to vary or revoke the order on the person's behalf` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 486.51(2) the court must vary or revoke the order without holding a hearing` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 486.51(2) the court must vary or revoke the order without holding a hearing` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- "unless the court is of the opinion that to do so may affect the privacy interests"
#ASSERT `s 486.51(2) the court must vary or revoke the order without holding a hearing` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- not made by the subject or someone acting for them (the accused, say)
#ASSERT `s 486.51(3) the court must hold a hearing to determine whether the order should be varied or revoked` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 486.51(3) the court must hold a hearing to determine whether the order should be varied or revoked` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 486.51(4) the court must take into account whether it is possible to vary the order in a manner that protects the privacy interests of any other person` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 486.51(4) the court must take into account whether it is possible to vary the order in a manner that protects the privacy interests of any other person` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- an application to revoke only
#ASSERT `s 486.51(5) the applicant is required to provide notice of the application to vary or revoke the order to the accused` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- "is not required"
#ASSERT `s 486.51(5) the applicant is required to provide notice of the application to vary or revoke the order to the accused` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 486.51(6) the accused is permitted to make submissions in relation to the application` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- "shall not be permitted"
#ASSERT `s 486.51(6) the accused is permitted to make submissions in relation to the application` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 486.51(7) the prosecutor must notify the accused` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 486.51(7) the prosecutor must notify the accused` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE

§ `s 486.6 -- offence, and the prosecutor's restraint`
#ASSERT `s 486.6(1) the order is one made under any of subsections 486.4(1) to (3) or subsection 486.5(1) or (2)` (`Provision of the Code` OF 486.4, "(1)")
#ASSERT `s 486.6(1) the order is one made under any of subsections 486.4(1) to (3) or subsection 486.5(1) or (2)` (`Provision of the Code` OF 486.4, "(2)")
#ASSERT `s 486.6(1) the order is one made under any of subsections 486.4(1) to (3) or subsection 486.5(1) or (2)` (`Provision of the Code` OF 486.4, "(2.1)")
#ASSERT `s 486.6(1) the order is one made under any of subsections 486.4(1) to (3) or subsection 486.5(1) or (2)` (`Provision of the Code` OF 486.4, "(2.2)")
#ASSERT `s 486.6(1) the order is one made under any of subsections 486.4(1) to (3) or subsection 486.5(1) or (2)` (`Provision of the Code` OF 486.4, "(3)")
#ASSERT NOT (`s 486.6(1) the order is one made under any of subsections 486.4(1) to (3) or subsection 486.5(1) or (2)` (`Provision of the Code` OF 486.4, "(3.1)"))
#ASSERT NOT (`s 486.6(1) the order is one made under any of subsections 486.4(1) to (3) or subsection 486.5(1) or (2)` (`Provision of the Code` OF 486.4, "(4)"))
#ASSERT `s 486.6(1) the order is one made under any of subsections 486.4(1) to (3) or subsection 486.5(1) or (2)` (`Provision of the Code` OF 486.5, "(1)")
#ASSERT `s 486.6(1) the order is one made under any of subsections 486.4(1) to (3) or subsection 486.5(1) or (2)` (`Provision of the Code` OF 486.5, "(2)")
#ASSERT NOT (`s 486.6(1) the order is one made under any of subsections 486.4(1) to (3) or subsection 486.5(1) or (2)` (`Provision of the Code` OF 486.5, "(3)"))
#ASSERT NOT (`s 486.6(1) the order is one made under any of subsections 486.4(1) to (3) or subsection 486.5(1) or (2)` (`Provision of the Code` OF 486.31, "(1)"))
#ASSERT `s 486.6(1) the person is guilty of an offence punishable on summary conviction` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 486.6(1) the person is guilty of an offence punishable on summary conviction` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 486.6(1) the person is guilty of an offence punishable on summary conviction` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING   -- an order the subsection does not name
#ASSERT `s 486.6(1) the punishment the section states`'s `mode` EQUALS `on summary conviction`
#ASSERT `s 486.6(1) the punishment the section states`'s `maximum imprisonment` EQUALS `no imprisonment is stated`
#ASSERT `s 486.6(1) the punishment the section states`'s `maximum fine` EQUALS `no fine is stated`
-- (1.1) the prosecutor shall not commence or continue a prosecution against the person who is the subject of the order unless, in their opinion, (a), (b) and (c)
#ASSERT `s 486.6(1.1) the prosecutor is barred from commencing or continuing a prosecution against the person who is the subject of the order` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 486.6(1.1) the prosecutor is barred from commencing or continuing a prosecution against the person who is the subject of the order` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- not knowingly
#ASSERT `s 486.6(1.1) the prosecutor is barred from commencing or continuing a prosecution against the person who is the subject of the order` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- no other person's privacy compromised
#ASSERT `s 486.6(1.1) the prosecutor is barred from commencing or continuing a prosecution against the person who is the subject of the order` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- a warning is appropriate
#ASSERT `s 486.6(1.1) the prosecutor is barred from commencing or continuing a prosecution against the person who is the subject of the order` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING   -- not the subject of the order
#ASSERT `s 486.6(2) the order applies to prohibit the publication of information that could identify a victim, witness or justice system participant in those proceedings` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 486.6(2) the order applies to prohibit the publication of information that could identify a victim, witness or justice system participant in those proceedings` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
